WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.304
Pydantic: one class, four jobs.

2
00:00:02.584 --> 00:00:10.456
Pydantic is a Python library that validates data against type hints (its docs describe it as the most widely used one).

3
00:00:10.736 --> 00:00:30.149
You declare a class whose attributes have types, and Pydantic gives you four things from that one declaration: a validator for incoming data, typed Python objects, a JSON Schema (from model_json_schema(), which targets Draft 2020-12), and documentation through field descriptions.

4
00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:45.000
The structured-output examples from Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, and xAI all accept a Pydantic model (directly, or through its generated schema), so the same class serves your prompt, your API call, and your tests.

5
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.885
That’s why you should treat the model class as the single source of truth.

6
00:00:49.165 --> 00:00:54.925
If the schema lives in a prompt string, a JSON file, and a parsing function, they’ll drift apart.

7
00:00:55.205 --> 00:00:58.171
If all three are generated from one class, they can’t.

8
00:00:58.451 --> 00:01:02.077
The building blocks map directly onto JSON Schema: Types.

9
00:01:02.357 --> 00:01:04.640
str, int, bool, datetime.

10
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.755
date, lists, and nested models.

11
00:01:07.035 --> 00:01:13.072
A date field parses “2026-11-20” into a real datetime.

12
00:01:13.352 --> 00:01:14.099
date.

13
00:01:14.379 --> 00:01:15.189
Enums.

14
00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:20.653
Literal["high", "medium", "low"] (or a Python Enum ) becomes a JSON Schema enum.

15
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:22.597
Required versus optional.

16
00:01:22.877 --> 00:01:25.181
A field with no default is required.

17
00:01:25.461 --> 00:01:27.616
A field with a default may be omitted.

18
00:01:27.896 --> 00:01:30.989
Allowing null is a separate choice: str | None.

19
00:01:31.269 --> 00:01:32.208
Constraints.

20
00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:38.504
Field(min_length=1), Field(ge=0), and friends add checks beyond the type.

21
00:01:38.784 --> 00:01:39.787
Descriptions.

22
00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.901
Field(description=".")

23
00:01:42.181 --> 00:01:43.440
lands in the schema.

24
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:47.261
Write descriptions as instructions to the model, because they are.

25
00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:48.672
Closed objects.

26
00:01:48.952 --> 00:01:56.717
model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid") rejects unknown keys and sets additionalProperties to false.
